EXTERNAL flag(name)
There is a new thing on your table: a disc of polished crystal in a bone frame, wrapped in a scrap of wool as if it might bite.
"Rune-lens," says Skögul. She is eating a smoked herring, bones and all. # speaker: skogul
"New decree. A warrior counts only with their own weapon. Pick up a friend's sword at the last moment and you die holding a friend's sword. Hel takes those." # speaker: skogul
"Good smiths cut the owner's name into the blade: 'Hallvard owns me.' Put the lens on it and read the name. If the name isn't theirs, the sword isn't either." # speaker: skogul
{ flag("asked_namesake"):
  "You asked me about names that match and faces that don't. This is the other way round. The face is theirs. The name on the blade isn't." # speaker: skogul
}
She pulls a sword from the pile behind her and lays it across the table, runes up. Along the blade, in Latin letters, it says +VLFBERHT+.
"The Franks make a sword called Ulfberht. The best steel there is. Every jarl wants one, so every smith in the north has started making them." # speaker: skogul
"The real ones put the cross between the H and the T. The copies put it at the end, where it looks right. That's how you know." # speaker: skogul
* ["Does a copy still count as their own weapon?"]
  "If they paid for it, it's theirs, and it counts. But they'll swear it's real, and that's a lie, and a caught lie is a ring." # speaker: skogul
* ["What happens to the smiths who made them?"]
  "The jarls are finding out this month. It's been a bad month to be a smith." # speaker: skogul
  She picks a bone out of her teeth and looks at it.
  "Your brother sweeps a smithy, doesn't he?" # speaker: skogul
- She wraps the lens back in its wool and pushes it across to you, as if she's glad to be rid of it.
-> END
